  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 1,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fquantization%2Fllm_compressor%2Fint8_w8a8.md",
      "changes": 2,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fquantization%2Fllm_compressor%2Fint8_w8a8.md?ref=5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor/int8_w8a8.md",
      "patch": "@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ Please visit the HF collection of [quantized INT8 checkpoints of popular LLMs re\n     INT8 computation is supported on NVIDIA GPUs with compute capability > 7.5 (Turing, Ampere, Ada Lovelace, Hopper).\n \n !!! warning\n-    **Blackwell GPU Limitation**: INT8 is not supported on compute capability >= 10.0 (e.g., RTX 6000 Blackwell).\n+    **Blackwell GPU Limitation**: INT8 is not supported on compute capability >= 10.0 (e.g., B200, GB200, RTX 6000 Blackwell, RTX 5090).\n     Use [FP8 quantization](fp8.md) instead, or run on Hopper/Ada/Ampere architectures.\n \n ## Prerequisites",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fquantization%2Fllm_compressor%2Fint8_w8a8.md",
      "sha": "4c60abd3bcecd7ce4953d75482ab4c8742beaf1a",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b/docs%2Fgetting_started%2Finstallation%2Fgpu.cuda.inc.md",
      "changes": 4,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Fgetting_started%2Finstallation%2Fgpu.cuda.inc.md?ref=5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "docs/getting_started/installation/gpu.cuda.inc.md",
      "patch": "@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ vLLM contains pre-compiled C++ and CUDA (12.9) binaries.\n --8<-- [end:installation]\n --8<-- [start:requirements]\n \n-- GPU: compute capability 7.5 or higher (e.g., T4, RTX20xx, A100, L4, H100, B200, etc.)\n+- GPU: compute capability 7.5 or higher (e.g., T4, RTX20xx, A100, L4, H100, B200, RTX 5090, etc.)\n \n --8<-- [end:requirements]\n --8<-- [start:set-up-using-python]\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ uv pip install vllm --torch-backend=auto\n We recommend leveraging `uv` to [automatically select the appropriate PyTorch index at runtime](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/guides/integration/pytorch/#automatic-backend-selection) by inspecting the installed CUDA driver version via `--torch-backend=auto` (or `UV_TORCH_BACKEND=auto`). To select a specific backend (e.g., `cu130`), set `--torch-backend=cu130` (or `UV_TORCH_BACKEND=cu130`). If this doesn't work, try running `uv self update` to update `uv` first.\n \n !!! note\n-    NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs (B200, GB200) require a minimum of CUDA 12.8, so make sure you are installing PyTorch wheels with at least that version. PyTorch itself offers a [dedicated interface](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/) to determine the appropriate pip command to run for a given target configuration.\n+    NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs (e.g., B200, GB200, RTX 5090) require a minimum of CUDA 12.8, so make sure you are installing PyTorch wheels with at least that version. PyTorch itself offers a [dedicated interface](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/) to determine the appropriate pip command to run for a given target configuration.\n \n As of now, vLLM's binaries are compiled with CUDA 12.9 and public PyTorch release versions by default. We also provide vLLM binaries compiled with CUDA 12.8, 13.0, and public PyTorch release versions:\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/5d41dc32785c2ea6e2300b2a03c019b5d124490b/docs%2Fgetting_started%2Finstallation%2Fgpu.cuda.inc.md",
      "sha": "6675c3565c60e83bdc6f5cbe8c468761373cffeb",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
